{
  "name": "483. A file named by its storage URI as an inference input belongs to the virtual key that uploaded it (storage-uri file ownership) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-7032. Local fixture regression, no live provider call: run with providerErrorFixture=1 against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, with tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs as the only upstream. A Vertex upload is recorded under its gs:// URI and a Bedrock upload under its s3:// URI, and a request can name that URI as an image, file, video or document input, which the provider then reads with the shared credential. Before TXE-7032 only a file_id and a Gemini file URL were read as naming an upload, so a second virtual key could have the model read the first key's object. Neither Vertex's nor Bedrock's host can be pointed at the fixture, so the provider here is an OpenAI-shaped stand-in (storage_uri_files, the fixture's /pp/storage) whose upload answers with a gs:// id: what the folder pins is the gateway's ownership check for that id form, which is the same code for every provider; it does not exercise Vertex's or Bedrock's own converters. 483.1 to 483.3 create two virtual keys and upload a file under the first. 483.4 to 483.9 name the upload's URI under the second key, as a chat image, with the scheme in upper case, as a Responses input image and input file, as an image edit input and inside an extra field: each is a 404 naming the file. 483.10 and 483.11 show the creating key is served and that a URI nobody uploaded is unrestricted. 483.12 reads what reached the provider: the upload and the two served chats, and none of the refused requests. The uploaded object is the fixture's and is not deleted; its URI is unique per upload.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "483.1 [setup] virtual key A (owner) on the storage-URI provider",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "  return;",
              "}",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('storageVkOwner'); pm.collectionVariables.unset('storageVkOwnerId');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('storageFileUri');",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__reset', method: 'POST' }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('the fixture was reset', function () { pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null); pm.expect(res.code).to.equal(200); });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the virtual key was created', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.equal(200); });",
              "var created = (pm.response.json() || {}).virtual_key || {};",
              "pm.test('it has an id and a value', function () { pm.expect(created.id, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); pm.expect(created.value, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); });",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('storageVkOwner', created.value || ''); pm.collectionVariables.set('storageVkOwnerId', created.id || '');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"name\": \"harness-483-a-{{$guid}}\", \"provider_configs\": [{\"provider\": \"storage_uri_files\", \"weight\": 1, \"allowed_models\": [\"*\"], \"key_ids\": [\"*\"]}]}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/governance/virtual-keys",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "governance",
            "virtual-keys"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
